&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a team of passionate and hardworking entrepreneurs to transform healthcare! Working in the tech team at Doctolib involves building innovative products and features to improve the daily lives of care teams and patients. We work in feature teams in an agile environment, while collaborating with engineering, design, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our Design System &amp;amp; Accessibility Team and help us become the #1 digital and secure medical companion for patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are part of the Platform domain, whose mission is to build and maintain the common building blocks of our system with a &quot;Platform as a Product&quot; mindset. We abstract and simplify the use of these complex, critical components, enabling product teams to focus on their core mission: building products faster for healthcare professionals and patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role matters:&lt;/strong&gt; With 80% of Doctolib&#39;s traffic coming from mobile, we&#39;re on a mission to bridge the gap between our Web and Mobile Design Systems. You&#39;ll be a key player in unifying the user experience across platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Frontend Platform team, we support and empower all other Doctolib Tech and Product teams to create Accessible and best-in-class user experience frontend applications. We achieve our mission by providing a web and mobile design system, by writing supporting tooling around it and the Accessibility topic, and guidance as Accessibility experts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain a scalable Web and mobile Design System built with React and React Native, ensuring a consistent, accessible, and high-performance user experience across Doctolib&#39;s web and mobile applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive the convergence of Web and Mobile Design Systems&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring visual and functional consistency across React and React Native components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and maintain React Native components&lt;/strong&gt;, enabling seamless cross-platform experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Upskill and mentor team members on React Native best practices&lt;/strong&gt;, fostering a culture of mobile-first thinking within the Design System team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hand-in-hand with Product Designers to translate Figma designs into robust, reusable UI components, ensuring visual and functional parity between design and code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion accessibility (A11y) by embedding inclusive design principles into our Design System, developing accessible components, and providing guidance and tooling to help product teams build compliant and user-friendly experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption and quality of the Design System by supporting teams, improving documentation, establishing usage guidelines, and gathering feedback to inform ongoing improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI technologies to amplify the Design System&#39;s adoption and developer experience (DevX), applying prompting and context engineering to create intelligent assistants, automation, and migration tools that help developers build user interfaces more efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally extend your impact beyond the frontend, improving scripts, build processes, or CI workflows that support efficient delivery of the Design System.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you don&#39;t meet all the requirements below but believe this opportunity matches your expectations and experience, we still encourage you to apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You could be our next team mate if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 5+ years of experience in Engineering;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have strong hands-on experience with React Native&lt;/strong&gt;, with a proven track record of building and shipping mobile applications;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong understanding of Design System architecture, component-driven development, and the collaboration between design and engineering;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have solid experience with React and TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt;, understanding the nuances between React Web and React Native development;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience applying or promoting Accessibility (A11y) best practices (WCAG, ARIA, semantic HTML, assistive technology testing);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are passionate about knowledge sharing and mentoring&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to upskill colleagues on mobile development;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the value of testing and code quality as foundations for scalable and robust interfaces;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to adapt and choose the most efficient technologies to solve complex UX and engineering challenges;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have proven experiences developing efficient, maintainable and secure products;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable speaking English in your day by day with the team;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now, it would be fantastic if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience building unified component libraries across Web and Mobile platforms;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a great understanding of JS/TS building and packaging processes;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a great understanding of web and mobile application performance tuning;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have native iOS or Android development experience alongside React Native;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have contributed to open-source mobile or Design System projects;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free comprehensive health insurance for you and your children&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parent Care Program: receive one additional month of leave on top of the legal parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free mental health and coaching services through our partner Moka.care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For caregivers and workers with disabilities, a package including an adaptation of the remote policy, extra days off for medical reasons, and psychological support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from abroad for up to 10 days per year thanks to our flexibility days policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work Council subsidy to refund part of sport club membership or creative class&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 14 days of RTT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch voucher with Swile card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiter Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feature Building interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System Design interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavioral Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offer!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Permanent Position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Levallois, Nantes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start Date: As soon as possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you would like to find out more about tech life at Doctolib, feel free to read our latest&lt;a href=&quot;https://medium.com/doctolib&quot;&gt; Medium blog articles&lt;/a&gt;!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Doctolib, we believe in improving access to healthcare for everyone - regardless of where you come from, what you look like. This translates into our recruitment process: Doctolib is an equal opportunity employer. We don&#39;t just accept diversity at Doctolib, we respect and celebrate it!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The more diverse ideas are heard, the more our product will truly improve healthcare for all. You are welcome to apply to Doctolib, regardless of your gender, religion, age, sexual orientation, ethnicity, disability, or place of origin. If you have a disability, let us know if there&#39;s any way we can make the interview process smoother for you!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;All the information transmitted via this form is processed by Doctolib for the purpose of managing applications. For more information on how Doctolib processes your application data, click&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://media.doctolib.com/image/upload/v1664533861/legal/Privacy-policy-Site_Career-Septembre-22-COM.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you wish to exercise your rights or if you have any questions about the processing of your data, you can write to us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;hr.dataprivacy@doctolib.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a team of passionate and hardworking entrepreneurs to transform healthcare!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in the tech team at Doctolib involves building innovative products and features to improve the daily lives of care teams and patients. We work in feature teams in an agile environment, while collaborating with product, design, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer FullStack&lt;/strong&gt; to join the FIRE (FHIR &amp;amp; Interoperability Requirements EHR) team&lt;strong&gt; in the Clinical domain&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, your mission will be to ensure that Doctolib DE is well connected to the German digital health ecosystem and compliant with FHIR standards. You will be responsible for the interoperability of the German EHR (Electronic Health Record): connection to the Telematik-Infrastruktur (TI), electronic prescriptions (eRezept), qualified electronic signature (QES), connected medical devices (GDT), and integration of laboratory results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the integration with German governmental health services, ensuring other Doctolib teams can seamlessly interact with the German health system through your platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the integration of the national EHR (Electronic Health Record) into Doctolib, with a multi-country rollout approach, navigating each country&#39;s standards and technical constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, ship, and operate production-grade fullstack solutions that connect the Doctolib platform to complex healthcare infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other engineering teams to shape the architecture of Doctolib&#39;s interoperability platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure privacy, security, and compliance by design in one of healthcare&#39;s most regulated technical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own performance, observability, and reliability: monitoring dashboards, SLO/SLI, and system health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to cross-functional initiatives that shape Doctolib&#39;s future interoperability strategy across Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our tech environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our solutions are built on a single, fully cloud-native platform that supports web and mobile app interfaces, multiple languages, and is adapted to country and healthcare specialty requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The FIRE team works on a FullStack scope: React / TypeScript on the frontend and Kotlin on the backend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our broader stack is composed of Rails, TypeScript, Java, Python, Kotlin, Swift, and React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We leverage AI ethically across our products to empower patients and health professionals. Discover our AI vision&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doctolib.com/ai-careers/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you convinced that you have exactly what it takes for the position? Then we encourage you to apply. Even if you don&#39;t meet every requirement, you might be exactly the right future Doctoliber for this or other positions!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you read on, if you don&#39;t have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 6+ years of experience as a software engineer, with strong &lt;strong&gt;fullstack expertise, particularly in Kotlin and React/TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of building robust, end-to-end solutions that balance technical excellence with intuitive user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to design systems (system design) and make sound architectural decisions in complex environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand and promote best practices related to the software development life cycle: automated testing, CI/CD, and DevOps practices (you build it, you run it)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are curious, autonomous, and have a taste for exploring new systems : you are comfortable solving problems without complete documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are at ease in complex technical environments with many external dependencies and evolving standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are eager to share your knowledge and help the team grow through pair programming and mentoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable speaking and writing in English in your day-to-day with the team, German is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Now, it would be fantastic if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with healthcare interoperability standards, particularly FHIR, HL7, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience integrating with governmental or regulated health systems (e.g. Telematik-Infrastruktur, eRezept, GDT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are familiar with the German digital health ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Deutschlandticket (Germany-wide public transport pass) fully paid for by Doctolib&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 vacation days + 1 additional day for each full calendar year of employment (up to a maximum of 30 days)&lt;/li&gt;
